> {{ r.headline }}

## 1. What was checked

For each resolution the AI claimed, the audit looked for a ticket from the same person in the following {{ r.settings.window_days }} days{% if r.settings.match == "same_type" %} about the same type of issue{% endif %}. The same check on tickets resolved by people{% if ret.standardized %}, weighted to the same issue mix{% endif %}, in the same weeks, gives the normal return rate. Only the excess counts against the AI:

did not hold = (return rate after the AI − return rate after people) ÷ (1 − return rate after people)

{{ lvl }}% ranges come from resampling people {{ r.settings.reps | num(0) }} times.

